module bindings.rust.modular_arithmetic_variable_time_division;

// Hardware integer division and remainder are variable-time in their operands
// on essentially every CPU, so applying either to a secret-dependent value
// leaks that value through the operation's duration. Constant-time
// arithmetic keeps every reduction on a fixed multiply-and-shift path --
// Barrett or Montgomery reduction, or a dedicated constant-time division
// helper -- which is the documented discipline of lattice and field
// implementations (the same reasoning the module_lattice algebra in
// RustCrypto/signatures states for its reduction moduli).
//
// The shape read here: a function that implements modular arithmetic and
// then divides or takes the remainder of a computed value in place with the
// compound operators /= or %= . The modular-arithmetic context is recognised
// by reduction vocabulary that is standard across arithmetic crates (mod_*,
// modulus, Barrett, Montgomery); a constant-time division helper named in
// the same function (ct_div, ct_rem, ct_reduce) is the neutralising control,
// because its presence is the shift-multiply replacement doing the work.
//
// Deliberately narrow in two directions. Only the compound operators carry
// the finding: the in-place form divides a value the function accumulated,
// while plain a / b in arithmetic code is overwhelmingly public bound and
// constant computation -- the sibling hint code in the same module computes
// public bounds with plain division and the module's own comment says so.
// And the context gate keeps ordinary averages, digit counting and tree
// index walks (size /= 2) out entirely: without reduction vocabulary the
// division is not field arithmetic. Residual: the match is over the
// function body, which carries comments, so a comment naming a constant-time
// helper suppresses -- the false-negative direction only.
binding modularArithmeticVariableTimeDivision {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "rust" and containsAny(node.token, ["/=", "%="]) and containsAny(node.token, ["mod_", "modulus", "Modulus", "Barrett", "barrett", "Montgomery", "montgomery"]) and not (containsAny(node.context.scopeCall, ["ct_div", "ct_rem", "ct_reduce"]))
  emit issue code.CryptoVariableTimeDivision at node
}
